# Line endings are decided here, not by whoever happens to commit.
#
# spotless is configured with <lineEndings>UNIX</lineEndings> in aud/pom.xml, and
# no published workflow runs spotless, so a CRLF file arriving from a Windows
# checkout would not be caught by anything downstream - it would simply fail the
# next `just fmt` for whoever ran it. Declaring the policy here makes git enforce
# it on the way in.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` stores LF in the repository and checks out LF on every
# platform. Every text file this project ships is fine with LF, including the
# shell and PowerShell scripts.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Files where a CRLF is an outright bug rather than a nuisance: a `#!` line with a
# trailing CR is not a valid interpreter path, and Docker copies bytes verbatim.
*.sh         text eol=lf
*.dockerfile text eol=lf
Dockerfile   text eol=lf
justfile     text eol=lf

# Better diff hunk headers for the language that makes up most of the repository.
*.java text diff=java

# Never normalise and never diff as text. Only logo.ico exists today; the rest are
# declared up front so a future asset cannot be quietly corrupted by the rule at
# the top of this file.
*.ico   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.pdf   binary
*.jar   binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
